-- CatMLM equivalent of MLM-USE/VehicleTaxonomy.use -- same domain, same
-- resolved model, terser surface syntax. Differences worth noticing:
--   - "category"/"class" fuses what plain MLM-USE splits across a model
--     block and a mediator block: Car's own shape AND the fact that it
--     instantiates Vehicle are both declared in Car's own "category ...
--     end" body (via the trailing "clabject Car : Vehicle" statement in
--     the same model block), not two separate MLM-USE-style blocks.
--   - CatMLM genuinely CANNOT express the plain-MLM-USE version's
--     "wheels -> wheelCount" rename, or per-clabject constraint removal --
--     catClabjectDefinition has no body at all beyond the powerclass list.
--     The only cancellation mechanism here is the "catConstr" tag, applied
--     once on PositiveWheels' own declaration -- it fires for every
--     instantiator of Vehicle, not selectively. That's why this version
--     keeps the attribute named "wheelCount" from the start, rather than
--     renaming it at the instantiation site.
--   - Operations still cannot be written in CatMLM at all (no "operations"
--     section in catClassifierDefinition) -- see MLM-USE/VehicleTaxonomy.use
--     for the version with isMultiTrack/isFamilyCar.

MLM VehicleTaxonomy

model M3
category Vehicle
attributes
wheelCount: Integer
end

constraints
context Vehicle inv PositiveWheels: catConstr
self.wheelCount > 0


model M2 < M3
category Car
attributes
seats: Integer
end

constraints
context Car inv ReasonableSeats:
self.seats > 0 and self.seats <= 9

clabject Car : Vehicle
end


model M1 < M2
class CarModel
attributes
modelYear: Integer
end

constraints
context CarModel inv ValidYear:
self.modelYear > 1900

clabject CarModel : Car
end
